			"notes": "**Download the one file for your Minecraft version and loader**, for example `desktopscreens-fabric-1.21.1-0.3.0.jar` for Fabric 1.21.1. Fabric needs Fabric API. Windows 10 (version 2004 or newer) and Windows 11. Also on CurseForge: https://www.curseforge.com/minecraft/mc-mods/desktop-screens\n\n**VR with Vivecraft** (every version except 1.12.2; Vivecraft 1.3 or newer):\n\n- Use a screen with your controllers: \"Use the screen\" shows your desktop on Vivecraft's floating panel, the same picture as on the screen in the world.\n- Point with the laser to move your mouse cursor. The trigger clicks; right-click and scrolling are on the same buttons as in your inventory.\n- Vivecraft's keyboard types into your PC. The menu button takes you back to the game.\n- Put \"Use the screen\" on a controller button once, in SteamVR's controller settings for Minecraft (the Mod section).\n- Vivecraft's \"Double GUI Resolution\" setting makes the desktop on the panel sharper.\n- Seated VR (no controllers) uses your mouse and keyboard, as on a PC.\n- VR support is new: please tell us what works and what doesn't.\n\n**Changes on every version:**\n\n- Hints show again whenever you look back at a screen, or at another part of it with the Screen Builder in hand (like \"Resize\" near an edge).\n- Turning a screen on says who sees it: \"Screen on: it shows your desktop to you and anyone you share it with\".\n\nPlease report bugs here on GitHub: https://github.com/MagiMigi/desktop-screens/issues"
		}
	],
	"readme": "README.md",
	"readmeSummary": "Your real PC desktop, inside Minecraft. Build a screen of any size in your base, turn it on, and it shows your desktop, live. Walk up to it, press G, and your real mouse and keyboard work on it.",
